WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.770
Here's how to load your clinic data
into the LUUMA dropout measurement app,

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.950
with two sample files.

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.170
This app measures treatment
dropout with the same definition

4
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.370
at every clinic in the network,
so results can be compared.

5
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.130
And everything is calculated
on your computer:

6
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.517
patient data is never sent anywhere.

7
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.770
Step one: prepare.

8
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.930
The app tells you which reports to ask
for, such as retrievals or transfers,

9
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.790
exactly as your system exports them.

10
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.483
Click Download the request, and give
it to whoever exports your data.

11
00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:33.390
This example uses two Excel files:

12
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.710
one with retrievals, and one
with transfers and outcomes.

13
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.130
They come with titles, two-row
headers and personal data.

14
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.183
No need to clean them: the app discards
names, IDs, emails and phone numbers.

15
00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.490
Step two: load.

16
00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.690
Click Start, then drag the files
in, or click to choose them.

17
00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.750
They're read on your
computer and never uploaded.

18
00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:58.070
Each file has its own card. It
shows which reports it brings:

19
00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.950
here, retrievals and
embryology by retrieval.

20
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.070
Then, how many columns
it recognized: 11 of 12.

21
00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.750
If it says Ready, there's nothing to do.

22
00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.190
To see how it was read,
click Review columns:

23
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.470
each item, with the column
it used and an example.

24
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.150
The medical record number is
replaced with an internal code,

25
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.550
and never leaves your computer.

26
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.950
Further down, how the values are read.

27
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.290
Biochemical is read as
Negative; Birth, as Live birth.

28
00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.450
If one is wrong, click Change.

29
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.850
If it all looks right,
click Confirm this report.

30
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.670
The app only asks what it can't decide.

31
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.190
Here, one thing: up to which
date the data are complete.

32
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.650
Choose the last record, September 30.

33
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.410
Below, the reports received: 4 of 5.

34
00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.683
Then click Verify the data.

35
00:01:46.203 --> 00:01:48.090
Step three: verify.

36
00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.690
A traffic light tells you
whether it can be calculated.

37
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.290
Green: ready for the report.

38
00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.970
Yellow: ready, with warnings
that explain part of the result.

39
00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.510
Red: something is missing;
it tells you what.

40
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.690
Here it's yellow: the
cryopreservation report is missing,

41
00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.870
so we don't know whether
embryos were left.

42
00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.583
It doesn't block: the
final report mentions it.

43
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.070
Step four: report and delivery.

44
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.370
Click See the report. At the top,
the main number: dropout per cycle.

45
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.270
In this example, 39.3%

46
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.050
of the cycles that can
already be evaluated.

47
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:22.010
Type the clinic's name: without
it, the download stays disabled.

48
00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.290
Click Download the Excel for LUUMA:

49
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.230
it has only counts and percentages, with small
groups hidden, and no dates or patient codes.

50
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.790
Copy the note for the email,
and send it with the Excel.

51
00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.650
The full report stays with
the clinic, as HTML or PDF.

52
00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:36.890
That's it.

53
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:43.117
If you have questions, the app has Help
and definition, with the complete rules.
